silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_03_pullback_vs_pushforward_sections_01_pushforward_as_information_flow_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'PushforwardAsInformationFlowConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, the pullback functor (sec 02). The bare math anchor-node name is resolved to a concrete household-or-clinic node of the Mittens vet-clinic transport scenario so a zero-math reader can ground the reading; the transport functor F preserves the typed arrows that bind this node into the larger commutative diagram.; also, a derived anchor for the transport diagram: the clinic-side image of the household typed leg, carrying composition data.." .
